          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പ്രചാരണം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പ്രചാരണം — pracāraṇaṁ — \"a campaign\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തിരഞ്ഞെടുപ്പ് പ്രചാരണം ഇന്നലെ അവസാനിച്ചു. tiraññeṭuppŭ pracāraṇaṁ innale avasāniccu. The election campaign ended yesterday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Campaigning is പ്രചാരണം (pracāraṇaṁ) നടത്തുക."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പ്രചാരണം (pracāraṇaṁ) is a learned word built on Sanskrit pracāra, \"coming forth, showing oneself; currency, usage\" (Monier-Williams), with the Sanskrit action-noun ending -aṇa: a campaign makes an idea current. Monier-Williams lists pracāraṇa itself only as \"scattering, strewing\", so the campaign sense is a modern one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
